# AGENTS.md

- Treat this as project-local guidance; follow more specific nested `AGENTS.md` files when present.
- Verify user claims against files, tests, or docs before changing code; name uncertainty and tradeoffs.
- Use red-green-refactor for features and bug fixes: reproduce behavior first, then make the smallest correct change.
- Keep infrastructure scripts and CI deterministic; prefer pinned versions and locked commands when the repo provides them.
- Preserve user-authored source and configuration during Forge-managed updates; change generated infrastructure only when required.
- Treat Forge-managed infrastructure as determined by the selected blueprint/options and Forge's printed `infrastructure:` summary; prefer changing the blueprint or running `forge sync` over hand-editing generated outputs.
- Make surgical edits: state assumptions, choose the smallest non-speculative change, match existing style, and avoid unrelated refactors, stale breadcrumbs, or duplicated repo documentation.
- Clean up only orphans created by your change; mention unrelated dead code instead of deleting it.
- Run the smallest relevant checks for touched code and report anything skipped.
- Update user-facing docs when behavior, setup, commands, or generated infrastructure changes.
